	(text "POTS AND GATE OUTPUTS"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 17.78 0)
		(effects
			(font (size 2.5 2.5) (bold yes))
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "134bd66c-4290-55b6-b868-75fb92baaaf2")
	)
	(text "Pots: MCP3208 on +3V3A. Its VREF and the pot tops share POT_REF (100 Ω + 10 µF from +3V3A), so readings are\nratiometric and the hand-wired pot leads can't disturb the DAC's supply. Each wiper: 1 kΩ + 100 nF, 1 MΩ to\nground so an unwired channel reads 0 (100 kΩ would bend a 100 kΩ pot's response by up to 12 %).\nGate outs: four, one per wiring bank (2026-10-16), from QA-QD of a 74HCT595 at 5 V (VIH 2.0 V, so 3.3 V logic drives\nit) → 1 kΩ → jack, BAV99 clamps to +5VD and GND. QE-QH are unused; QH' still chains a second 595 from J603.\nOE is held high (outputs off) by a pull-up until firmware drives GATE_OE_N low: the 595's register powers up random."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 22.86 0)
		(effects
			(font (size 1.5 1.5))
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "84360ef9-de11-5dff-961a-ce82433d6cfc")
	)
